 `comp-draw-node` handled five of the seven widget kinds and answered
 `otherwise -> 0` for `WkInput` and `WkCustom`. A widget that lays out,
 occupies its space and paints nothing reads as a layout bug rather than
 as a missing arm, which is why it survived: the tree looked right and the
 pixels were simply absent. This pins both arms.

 **The measurement is a DIFFERENCE against a baseline, and the first cut
 of this test got that wrong.** It rendered one tree and counted non-zero
 cells inside the child's bounds. Every cell in the buffer is non-zero,
 because the root panel fills the whole rectangle before any child paints,
 so that counted the panel and answered the same thing whatever the child
 did. Here each arm renders twice -- a root with no children, then the
 same root with the child -- and counts the cells that CHANGED. That is
 the child's own contribution and nothing else.

 The gauge is the calibration. It was drawn before this change, so it must
 register under exactly this harness; if its row ever reads `no` the
 harness is broken and the rows above it are answering a question nobody
 asked.

 `event-dot` is counted exactly: six by six is 36 cells, so a dot drawn at
 the wrong size or in the wrong place fails on the number rather than on a
 yes.

 **Fired against the arms removed** (`otherwise -> 0` restored, seed
 37A7EF8E4EF603AE): `input painted` and `event-dot is 6 by 6` both go to
 `no` and the gauge control holds. `input inside its box` stays `yes`
 under that sabotage and it is worth saying why rather than counting it as
 a third moved row: with nothing painted both counts are zero and zero
 equals zero. It is meaningful only while `input painted` reads yes, which
 is the row it is paired with.

 The unknown-tag fallback is deliberately NOT asserted here. It fills its
 bounds with the panel style, `widget-resolve-style` gives a `WkCustom`
 the same panel style as its parent, and painting a colour over the same
 colour changes no cell. It is unobservable by difference, and a row that
 cannot fail is worse than an absent one.

 We say:

Section: Geometry

  ck-w : Integer = 200
  ck-h : Integer = 40
  ck-cells : Integer = 8000
  ck-bytes : Integer = 32000

Section: Counting

  zero-fill : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zero-fill (b) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0 else let p = poke-32 b i 0 in zero-fill b (i + 4) n

  changed-at : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  changed-at (a) (b) (i) = if peek-32 a (i * 4) /= peek-32 b (i * 4) then 1 else 0

  count-changed : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-changed (a) (b) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else count-changed a b (i + 1) n (acc + changed-at a b i)

  changed-cols : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  changed-cols (a) (b) (x) (xend) (y) (acc) =
    if x >= xend then acc
    else changed-cols a b (x + 1) xend y (acc + changed-at a b (y * ck-w + x))

  changed-box : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  changed-box (a) (b) (x0) (y0) (bw) (bh) (y) (acc) =
    if y >= bh then acc
    else changed-box a b x0 y0 bw bh (y + 1) (changed-cols a b x0 (x0 + bw) (y0 + y) acc)

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

Section: Trees

  ck-bare : WidgetNode
  ck-bare = widget-panel "root" DirColumn 0 []

  ck-input : WidgetNode
  ck-input = widget-panel "root" DirColumn 0 [widget-input "field" "abc" 3]

  ck-dot : WidgetNode
  ck-dot = widget-panel "root" DirColumn 0 [widget-custom "dot" "event-dot" 20 20]

  ck-gauge : WidgetNode
  ck-gauge = widget-panel "root" DirColumn 0 [widget-gauge "g" 1 2]

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let font = cbf-init
    in let th = theme-terminal
    in let base = __heap-save
    in let adv = __heap-advance (2 * ck-bytes + 256)
    in let subj = base + ck-bytes
    in act

 The baseline is painted once: the root alone, no children. Every arm
 below is the same root with one child added, so any cell that differs
 from this buffer was written by that child.

      let zb = zero-fill base 0 ck-bytes
      in let rb = comp-render base ck-w font ck-bare th ck-w ck-h

      in let z0 = zero-fill subj 0 ck-bytes
      in let r0 = comp-render subj ck-w font ck-input th ck-w ck-h
      in let k0 = (list-at (r0.wn-children) 0).wn-bounds
      in let all0 = count-changed base subj 0 ck-cells 0
      in let box0 = changed-box base subj (k0.lr-x) (k0.lr-y) (k0.lr-w) (k0.lr-h) 0 0

      in let z1 = zero-fill subj 0 ck-bytes
      in let r1 = comp-render subj ck-w font ck-dot th ck-w ck-h
      in let all1 = count-changed base subj 0 ck-cells 0

      in let z2 = zero-fill subj 0 ck-bytes
      in let r2 = comp-render subj ck-w font ck-gauge th ck-w ck-h
      in let all2 = count-changed base subj 0 ck-cells 0

      in act
        print-line-uni ("input painted        : " & yn (all0 > 0))
        print-line-uni ("input inside its box : " & yn (box0 == all0))
        print-line-uni ("event-dot is 6 by 6  : " & yn (all1 == 36))
        print-line-uni ("gauge painted (ctrl) : " & yn (all2 > 0))
      end
    end
  end

